WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:04.154
Steps one to six run in
the non-person identity

3
00:00:04.154 --> 00:00:07.000
folder of the examples, in PowerShell 7.

4
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.184
Step one runs Microsoft's Sentinel
rule for new app credentials,

5
00:00:11.184 --> 00:00:16.237
the one Microsoft Learn's security
operations guide for applications links,

6
00:00:16.237 --> 00:00:19.158
over the fixture: eleven
tests pass, none fail,

7
00:00:19.158 --> 00:00:22.000
and forty of the file's
other tests aren't run.

8
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.102
Step two lists what the run needs:
four Graph read permissions,

9
00:00:26.102 --> 00:00:29.963
Application, AuditLog, Directory
and User dot Read dot All.

10
00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:31.637
Nothing ends in ReadWrite.

11
00:00:31.637 --> 00:00:36.799
Step three runs the first day, the
twenty-ninth of October, with no baseline.

12
00:00:36.799 --> 00:00:41.826
Inventory, ownership and drift all report
OK, and the run becomes a baseline

13
00:00:41.826 --> 00:00:44.177
candidate, with fourteen findings,

14
00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:47.825
four warnings and five
information items, and its hash.

15
00:00:47.825 --> 00:00:52.100
Step four approves that baseline by
its hash and runs the second day.

16
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.740
It compares with the first day's baseline,

17
00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:58.750
and the drift appears: eighteen
findings and eleven warnings.
